{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone","id":1015553,"title":"Rome for Everyone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-10T22:42:31-08:00","id":1015553,"title":"Rome for Everyone","content":"I swear I've already made this thread somewhere (and if I had, please link me to it), but...<br /> <br /> <i>Requiem for Rome</i> ostensibly covered the whole empire from a Kindred perspective, but definitely focused on the city herself; the chapters in the <i>Dark Eras Companion</i> will give a barbarian (I believe Germania is the focus, but I could be forgetting?) provinces a Forsaken view, while the Mummy content will do the obvious and drill down into Aegyptus. But Rome was vast, and the CofD has so many more gamelines to cover, so I was curious to hear which areas everyone here would like to see should every gameline get the Roman treatment!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:03:04-08:00","id":1015563,"title":"","content":"Can we just get a Dark Eras: Rome? Just a whole Dark Eras sized book of nothing but Ancient Rome, each line gets a chapter. I would pay all of the monies for that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-11-2016, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:10:40-08:00","id":1015568,"title":"","content":"Fun Fact: Changeling 1E posited the Seasonal Courts officially started at some time in the Roman Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:12:05-08:00","id":1015569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015563#post1015563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we just get a Dark Eras: Rome? Just a whole Dark Eras sized book of nothing but Ancient Rome, each line gets a chapter. I would pay all of the monies for that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would get my money <i>and</i> my blood sacrifice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 12-11-2016, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:53:16-08:00","id":1015576,"title":"","content":"The <i>Dark Eras Companion</i> chapter covers more than just barbarians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T00:20:22-08:00","id":1015582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015576#post1015576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>Dark Eras Companion</i> chapter covers more than just barbarians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, goody! Does it focus on a particular area like I assumed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T00:20:49-08:00","id":1015583,"title":"","content":"I think a Dark Eras style look at the 2nd Punic War would be cool, especially in how it effected the Camarilla and the other supernatural cultures. <br /> <br /> After learning about the actual event it left a lot to be desired from what was presented in OWofD, and Requiem for Rome already did such a good job at handling roman culture. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T00:45:34-08:00","id":1015590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015576#post1015576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>Dark Eras Companion</i> chapter covers more than just barbarians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really glad to hear that. It's a stereotype and I think a lot of people get stuck to them when coming to the game because of reinforcements like that.<br /> <br /> I believe the writer posts here occasionally and has gotten me enthused with what little they've been able to share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-11-2016, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:10:34-08:00","id":1015610,"title":"","content":"I have a half-finished Vigil for Rome project I should reopen.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> I replaced the official version of the Aves Minerva because I found them too much &quot;generic Roman pagans&quot; which works when they're the only Hunter group in the setting, but if they're sharing it with other Roman Hunters they need to be more distinct. Quick run down of the groups I decided to focus on...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Compacts</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Aves Minerva: Plebs and Freemen defenders of the streets of the city. More like the Union than any other modern Compact. They've always been patriotically dedicated to the gods of the city, but debate rages over the admittance of Christians.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Mos Maiorum: Patricians protecting the honor of their families from the blight of the walking dead or other accursed stigmas</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Vox Martyom: Heretical Christians of the Agonistici tradition, who believe martyrdom is the only path to salvation. As the state doesn't serve that purpose anymore post-Constantine, they turn their attention to the unholy forces in the shadows</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Conspiracies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Collegia Chironos: A mystery cult primarily made up of educated Greek slaves, seeking knowledge of the medical and mystical</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Ieros Dromos: Nicean Christians answerable to Constantinople, breaking the power of the Gnostic witches and the cults of pagan horrors to save the souls of the masses</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Lux Mithrae: a Conspiracy within the Legions wielding consecrated blood of the bull against supernatural foes of the Empire (this is where the Red Rites move)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Other groups (like the Ascending Ones who are the premier Hunters in the Parthian Empire at this point) get some sidebar attention.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:15:27-08:00","id":1015614,"title":"","content":"Based on 1E <b>Mage</b> materials, I proposed post 2nd Punic War Rome as place of final hammering of Diamond Orders from Darshanas on West. And early Empire era as birth place of Seers of Throne as Order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More to read in this topic: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">History of Awakened</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-11-2016, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:22:32-08:00","id":1015615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015590#post1015590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm really glad to hear that. It's a stereotype and I think a lot of people get stuck to them when coming to the game because of reinforcements like that.<br /> <br /> I believe the writer posts here occasionally and has gotten me enthused with what little they've been able to share.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let me think back on what's already been said. The era focuses on extra-territorial expansion, and Germania is most important for the selected time. *But*, it provides enough detail about Rome to understand the politics and tensions and play anywhere in the Empire. Also, as was <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">already teased by Stew Wilson</a>, it includes rules for playing the Pure. So read into that what you will...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T04:19:42-08:00","id":1015638,"title":"","content":"Mmmm.... [redacted].<br /> <br /> Mothers be praised!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T06:19:30-08:00","id":1015654,"title":"","content":"As for Roman Werewolf - I want just recall my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=272764#post272764\">fan created Roman Uratha myth</a>. I'm more than eager to see how much I was right with <b>Dark Eras Companion</b> stuff even 2,5 years before it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=272764#post272764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Roman Uratha</b><br /> So lately I was thinking about other alternative Uratha local myths variant \u2013 Roman werewolves. In legend of Rome\u2019s foundation myth <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romulus_and_Remus\" target=\"_blank\">Romulus and Remus</a> are first builders of the city. They are sons of mortal women (Rea Silvia/ IIla, Vestal Virigin ) and war god Mars. But after killing they mother, they are taken under auspice ( pun intended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) of Capitoline Wolf and when they are much stronger they return to human civilization. Years later they make a town, kill the murderes of their mother and come in to fratricidal conflict. It\u2019s what humans says.<br /> <br /> For Uratha tale would be much simpler \u2013 <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitoline_Wolf\" target=\"_blank\">Capitoline Wolf</a> would be twins biological and spiritual mother ( as Mother Wolf figure ). And they father should be lunar deity. Problem is that in Roman mythology there is Moon goddess <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luna_(goddess)\" target=\"_blank\">Luna</a>, not god. So how to solve this dilemma \u2013 Uratha are children of two female spirits? Or maybe they are children of Mars, not Luna?<br /> <br /> Fratricidal conflict would, of course, be about first pack in fighting and dividing on Forsaken and Pure \u2013 but what side would choose what brother? Is it Romulus or Remus more Forsaken patron?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:49:15-08:00","id":1015733,"title":"","content":"well, I have wrote a couple of Roman groups, and I have some thoughts for a Demon/Hunter/Mummy Punic Wars Dark Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:53:13-08:00","id":1015736,"title":"","content":"In my personal take of Roman Uratha, they got rid of Father Wolf's myth altogether. Instead, they believe in the Capitoline Wolf as a powerful spiritual entity that choose the demigod twins and turned them in the first Uratha. For them, the Uratha race came from Rome and spread, and the other myths are just barbarian bullshit. Indeed, one of the worst decision in history was to have children or otherwise spread their blessings with barbarians.<br /> <br /> My modern Rome setting have the local werewolves go as far as to form their own Tribes, with their own patron spirits of Roman mythology. They're not Forsaken nor Pure, they're Patricians, and be damned any &quot;evidence&quot; on the contrary. By the way, they learn the Spirit Tongue as everyone else, but see it as demeaning and meant only to talk with lowly spirits. Most learn classical Latim for their rites and formal affairs, and roman spirits learned to do so as well when they wish to be able to communicate with the Uratha, which only serves to convince further the Patricians that they are right about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T11:36:23-08:00","id":1015746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015736#post1015736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my personal take of Roman Uratha, they got rid of Father Wolf's myth altogether. Instead, they believe in the Capitoline Wolf as a powerful spiritual entity that choose the demigod twins and turned them in the first Uratha. For them, the Uratha race came from Rome and spread, and the other myths are just barbarian bullshit. Indeed, one of the worst decision in history was to have children or otherwise spread their blessings with barbarians.<br /> <br /> My modern Rome setting have the local werewolves go as far as to form their own Tribes, with their own patron spirits of Roman mythology. They're not Forsaken nor Pure, they're Patricians, and be damned any &amp;quot;evidence&amp;quot; on the contrary. By the way, they learn the Spirit Tongue as everyone else, but see it as demeaning and meant only to talk with lowly spirits. Most learn classical Latim for their rites and formal affairs, and roman spirits learned to do so as well when they wish to be able to communicate with the Uratha, which only serves to convince further the Patricians that they are right about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I play at your table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T11:57:08-08:00","id":1015757,"title":"","content":"This setting was used twice, already, but not currently. If you want, I can invite you when I start another Forsaken game with it.<br /> <br /> Just have to say: it is Play by Skype and, well, most of my current players don't speak english, only portuguese.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:00:19-08:00","id":1015759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015736#post1015736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most learn classical Latim for their rites and formal affairs, and roman spirits learned to do so as well when they wish to be able to communicate with the Uratha, which only serves to convince further the Patricians that they are right about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good thing then that most Italians have to learn Latin in high school!<br /> I'd really like to know more about your setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, I'm torn on the idea. I <i>love</i> Requiem for Rome, but the more Ancient Rome there is, the less chance I have to see modern Rome as a city in a new edition corebook. And I'm greedy for more Rome, it's my hometown!<br /> Still, I would like the Gallic Wars see a good treatment. It's a pretty short period, from 58 to 50 BCE, but it's one ripe of plot opportunities: never mind the obvious werewolves and vampire invaders vs the &quot;barbarian&quot; supernaturals. I want to see more druids. As in &quot;Awakened Druids&quot;. Were they as fond of human sacrifices as Julius Caesar described in the Bello Gallico, or were they painted this way to demonize them? Maybe they were part of one of the last better organized Scelesti communities.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the wicked men were part of a ritual to create Prometheans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:08:51-08:00","id":1015764,"title":"","content":"We managed to cover a lot of history, and a few legends, but couldn't go into great detail. And that's a shame cuz there's so much awesome Roman history that can be matched with W:tF ideas, and Rome deserves the Uratha treatment just as much (if not more so) than the Vampire treatment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:20:33-08:00","id":1015769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015736#post1015736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my personal take of Roman Uratha, they got rid of Father Wolf's myth altogether. Instead, they believe in the Capitoline Wolf as a powerful spiritual entity that choose the demigod twins and turned them in the first Uratha. For them, the Uratha race came from Rome and spread, and the other myths are just barbarian bullshit. Indeed, one of the worst decision in history was to have children or otherwise spread their blessings with barbarians.<br /> <br /> My modern Rome setting have the local werewolves go as far as to form their own Tribes, with their own patron spirits of Roman mythology. They're not Forsaken nor Pure, they're Patricians, and be damned any &quot;evidence&quot; on the contrary. By the way, they learn the Spirit Tongue as everyone else, but see it as demeaning and meant only to talk with lowly spirits. Most learn classical Latim for their rites and formal affairs, and roman spirits learned to do so as well when they wish to be able to communicate with the Uratha, which only serves to convince further the Patricians that they are right about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>do you mind posting some of your setting material? It sounds awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:36:48-08:00","id":1015780,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3765_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3765\" data-vbnamecard=\"3765\">SNESferatu</a>, I didn't know about it, though it makes sense. Let me ask: how much people actually learn it for more than just passing tests? I'm actually curious. I remember your thread about modern Rome, it was the first one where I posted in the forum, and it got me rethinking this setting since. Your advice is welcome.<br /> <br /> By the way, I also expect material for modern Rome. I find it far more interesting to deliver modern with just a hint to the past, than to make so much material about the past outright. Not that I'm against games set in the past, I just find it more interesting as a development policy for the setting. It makes the past mysterious even giving material to work, make it simpler to use the modern setting and let the ST adapt the hints better to a personal take in ancient history.<br /> <br /> The Gallic Wars are great, and full of mysteries by themselves, since we only have good descriptions of the Gauls coming from greatly unreliable sources. The druids can be a lot of interesting things, and given the tribal nature of the Gauls, they can be more than one thing at once.<br /> <br /> Even then, it would be interesting to have the Gallic Wars and the Gaul society tackled from a modern perspective in the books. Something about the effects of both the past and its legends in the current supernatural societies of the region, their theories and, maybe, some ruins and relics of this past.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"167\" data-vbnamecard=\"167\">nikink</a>, the take on Rome is a relic from WoD, in two ways. First, Vampire was the game line that most dealt with ancient history in WoD, so Rome was &quot;their turf&quot;. Werewolf dealt more with pre-history, and them with very recent events. Mage is the main source in the Middle Ages (curiously even more than Vampire Dark Ages, setting-wise). It IS a simplification, of course, but this focus carried over. Then they decided to link the Camarilla with Rome in the core book of Requiem 1st edition, and that was it. Rome become iconic in Requiem, while other game lines kind of went through other waters. It is a shame, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:05:59-08:00","id":1015797,"title":"","content":"I hope I'm not too off topic...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015780#post1015780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3765_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3765\" data-vbnamecard=\"3765\">SNESferatu</a>, I didn't know about it, though it makes sense. Let me ask: how much people actually learn it for more than just passing tests? I'm actually curious. I remember your thread about modern Rome, it was the first one where I posted in the forum, and it got me rethinking this setting since. Your advice is welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what kind of high school you were in, we have lots. The most popular are the Classico and the Scientifico. The Classico is the one with the most &quot;prestige&quot;, but times are changing and nobody cares about humanities anymore, so it's losing some of its &quot;status&quot;. Classico high schoolers learn Latin <i>and</i> Ancient Greek, and are the most versed in them. Still, probably not enough.<br /> I studied in a Scientifico. As the name says, it's mainly focused on maths and sciences, but Latin was super duper important there, too. Of five years of high school, two are spent learning grammar (and translating random stuff), and three studying, reading and translating classical works, mainly Cicero's and Caesar's.<br /> Most other schools have abandoned the study of the language, but the vast majority of people have some passing knowledge of it. And they have probably hated every single minute of that.<br /> <br /> Problem is, the way Latin is taught is much more akin to a puzzle than a language, and that's a shame. I mean, we suck at English too, but that's on a whole different level. You cannot translate <i>anything</i> without a dictionary. The classic Latin test is the <i>versione</i>, aka translating 12 or so lines from Latin to Italian, in two hours. It's a pain, and most people are rubbish at it. I was the best at it in my class, but my Latin is franky non-existent.<br /> <br /> So, your werewolves will probably know <i>how</i> the language works, but not <i>how to actually use it</i>. They cannot read it, but they have no issue with spellingand pronunciation.<br /> PS: Ancient Romans and Latin have a very strong link with the Fascist Regime, for obvious reasons. I expect lots of confusion between your packs and the various far-right groups of Rome...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:40:51-08:00","id":1015854,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3765_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3765\" data-vbnamecard=\"3765\">SNESferatu</a>, I was already thinking of strong links between most of the fiercest Patricians and far-right groups. In the end, the Patricians are mostly your average nationalists, and most packs are indeed grounded on actual roman politics.<br /> <br /> What I'm not sure is how to tackle it in the mundane side. Of course, being a Brazilian without any link to actual Italy, my knowledge of the details of current politics in your city is limited, to say the least. But on the other side, fiction demands fiction, and maybe my ignorance can help by actually forcing me to create parties and such instead of leaning too much on personal readings on actual ones.<br /> <br /> But what would you recommend? And there is something you can talk about this subject that you think would help?<br /> <br /> Oh, and probably most of them will rely on Latim learned from school, anyway, maybe with more pride than it deserves. And I can picture a certain contention between scholars that defend the current take on pronunciation, and revisionists based on recent theories of how ancient high-class Romans actually talked.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, it will take some time to find the material, but yeah, I'll share when I find. What I can present for now, though...<br /> <br /> First, it should be clear that the Patricians aren't necessarily an ancient phenomena. Maybe their origins are in ancient Rome indeed, but their current form is quite a modern phenomena. They aren't from classical times, they are just modern classicists.<br /> <br /> I thought of the Patricians liking very much the notion of <i>Lares</i>, ancient spirit protectors of Roman streets, buildings and landmarks, and linking their Totems to that notion, instead. The most powerful &quot;Lares&quot; are the patrons of the Patrician &quot;Tribes&quot;. I had found a proper terminology for Tribe, but forgot it by now. The use (not necessarily correct) of Latim instead of shamanistic or First Tongue terms will be an obvious development.<br /> <br /> The Tribes divided pretty much on general views of the Roman society. One is founded over the notion of the Legionnaire as a glorified servitor of the city. Under 2nd edition they would probably declare Sacred Hunt on the enemies of the city of Rome (as they perceive it, of course). Another is about the Caesars, about rulership of the city and of &quot;lesser citizens&quot;, probably being receptive to &quot;barbarians&quot; in their own way. Sacred Hunt could be aimed to keep the power structure, though I accept suggestions (for everything, actually). There is one about Roman scholars, devoted to learn and keep the civil traditions of Rome, and two religious tribes at each other's throats, a Cristian one and a Pagan one, dedicated each not only to their religions, but to what they represent to the Eternal City.<br /> <br /> As you can see, the Patricians are incredibly devoted and structured around the city itself. Some still dream of expansion, delivering the Light of Rome to the bleak barbarian world. Others defend that it was the ultimate downfall of their empire into crisis, and that Rome should focus on itself. They are obsessed with purity of the Roman blood, which also means that some are Patricians only because they are from Patrician families, or otherwise of &quot;pure&quot; Roman blood and decided to keep with kin, while others are outright fascists and xenophobes. Their territories, for now, both comprise the city and metropolitan area itself as wild and farm areas around it.<br /> <br /> Patricians aren't the only Uratha in Rome, either. There are both Forsaken and Pure in the area, making for quite complex interactions. Since Patricians only accept &quot;true&quot; Romans among them, werewolves that don't get acceptance have to seek the common tribes, that aren't as present because of the Patrician Tribes. The requisites to be considered a True Roman aren't that well defined, either, which lends more room for conflict when a given werewolf is accepted as a member of a given Tribe, but other werewolf don't consider this a valid decision.<br /> <br /> Conflicts in Rome, so, are characterized by lineage and beliefs taking precedence. People fight over romanticized perceptions of things, be it past, blood, religion. They don't fight so much over things, but mostly over how each interpret those things. A lot of Patricians will sense more kinship with cursed undead, otherworldly fairies, and other, stranger, things, if they have personal reason to think those as &quot;true Romans&quot;, than with a fellow Uratha that came from Sicily.<br /> <br /> Just to finish for now, the Patricians do have a common meeting ground, their greatest institution. The Forum. They deem the Shadow of the ancient Forum Romanum as neutral and sacred meeting ground, a place where every Patrician can have a voice, share news and opinions, where physical and mystical fights are forbidden, but vicious political fights are deadly. By force of law this place is protected by all Packs when needed, and at least one Pack is tasked to stay and guard at all times. It is maintained by alliance with local spirits that reflect the Patrician view of the city, and other spirits, along with any &quot;barbarian&quot; that somehow manages to approach it by the Shadow, are expeled with extreme violence after only one warning if that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T17:11:11-08:00","id":1015903,"title":"","content":"Requiem for Rome is my favorite CofD book(right next to Damnation City). I would totally love to get a Dark Eras: Rome book.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T20:25:05-08:00","id":1015958,"title":"","content":"It comes to me that I dearly wish I knew enough about the Jewish revolts to pitch a Promethean setting tied into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T04:19:23-08:00","id":1016053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015958#post1015958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It comes to me that I dearly wish I knew enough about the Jewish revolts to pitch a Promethean setting tied into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>ammm.. among the three Revolts, I personally think that the Bar Kokhba revolt is the most interesting one to explore, especially that as the last one it was built upon the two former ones, and I have personally always found Bar Kokhba as an interesting historical character. I think that if I were to link it to Promethean, it may be thought as a &quot;failed New Dawn&quot;- that is, the jewish people of the time have already saw themselves on the path of becoming an independent nation- only for their hope to be crushed so lowly, that it literally sent the jewish diaspora to a 2000 years of &quot;pilgrimage&quot;. If anything, I think that the pre-Frankenstein fire based Lineage of prophets and martyrs should be dominant at that Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T15:09:04-08:00","id":1016268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015610#post1015610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a half-finished Vigil for Rome project I should reopen.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> I replaced the official version of the Aves Minerva because I found them too much &quot;generic Roman pagans&quot; which works when they're the only Hunter group in the setting, but if they're sharing it with other Roman Hunters they need to be more distinct. Quick run down of the groups I decided to focus on...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Compacts</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Aves Minerva: Plebs and Freemen defenders of the streets of the city. More like the Union than any other modern Compact. They've always been patriotically dedicated to the gods of the city, but debate rages over the admittance of Christians.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Mos Maiorum: Patricians protecting the honor of their families from the blight of the walking dead or other accursed stigmas</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Vox Martyom: Heretical Christians of the Agonistici tradition, who believe martyrdom is the only path to salvation. As the state doesn't serve that purpose anymore post-Constantine, they turn their attention to the unholy forces in the shadows</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Conspiracies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Collegia Chironos: A mystery cult primarily made up of educated Greek slaves, seeking knowledge of the medical and mystical</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Ieros Dromos: Nicean Christians answerable to Constantinople, breaking the power of the Gnostic witches and the cults of pagan horrors to save the souls of the masses</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Lux Mithrae: a Conspiracy within the Legions wielding consecrated blood of the bull against supernatural foes of the Empire (this is where the Red Rites move)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Other groups (like the Ascending Ones who are the premier Hunters in the Parthian Empire at this point) get some sidebar attention.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea for the Aves Minerva, but I'd sooner see that concept tied into the <i>vigiles</i> while the Aves Minerva are free to be tied to her cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T15:44:19-08:00","id":1016282,"title":"","content":"I'd also love a Dark Eras Rome book (or better still, a series of books, as the gameline of that year). I'd offer my primogen in order to get that.<br /> <br /> for mage it could be the age when Orders form in its current form: After some centuries of existence, withe the roman conquest of Greece, Middle East and Egypt, the Darshanas expand for the Roman empire, and begin to institutionalize themselves, becoming magical Orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:47:40-08:00","id":1016316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1016282#post1016282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also love a Dark Eras Rome book (or better still, a series of books, as the gameline of that year). I'd offer my primogen in order to get that.<br /> <br /> for mage it could be the age when Orders form in its current form: After some centuries of existence, withe the roman conquest of Greece, Middle East and Egypt, the Darshanas expand for the Roman empire, and begin to institutionalize themselves, becoming magical Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canonically, I believe this is when the Seers crystalize into a proper Order instead of a bunch of independent Exarch cults, so that could be fun to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T21:04:16-08:00","id":1016391,"title":"","content":"I'd actually like a series of books for all gamelines that fleshes out not just the Roman Era but across the whole world at that time. So, very much like the Dark Eras book, but the time is fixed to approximately the Roman Republic (give or take a century) while the gamelines switch the geographical region covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:42:03-08:00","id":1016450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1016282#post1016282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for mage it could be the age when Orders form in its current form: After some centuries of existence, withe the roman conquest of Greece, Middle East and Egypt, the Darshanas expand for the Roman empire, and begin to institutionalize themselves, becoming magical Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">proposed two years before now</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook points that Adamantine Arrow was created around year 200 BCE - for me, it should be just end of 1st Punic War, where Arrows would be Roman Legion Darshana cult that won the conflict and as victors, come back to Rome to defined Republic and become first Western Caucus. So Arrows would become Roman faction more around 241 BCE, and rest of Diamond quickly follow them on this paradigm shift. Till the 2nd Punic War ( started at 218 BCE ) all five caucuses Orders would take shape as we know it. After 2nd war with Carthage, Arrows would recruit next mages from lands Roman Legions take recruits, so they would spread on as proper, global Order. Rest of Diamond follow model and by the the end of 3rd Punic War ( around 148 BCE ) we would have semi-globalized Diamond Orders of modern era.<br /> <br /> First Consilium of Rome I pointed at around 121-59 BCE, with rising unrests in proper city and small revolts. First Ruling Council would be based on Hierarch idea from Arcadian Mysteries traditions to solve infightings in Roman Diamond society, leading to slow spreading of system in Republic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1016316#post1016316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically, I believe this is when the Seers crystalize into a proper Order instead of a bunch of independent Exarch cults, so that could be fun to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>1E <b>Guardians of Veil</b> book points that Seers of Throne were uncovered at start of Empire, around 27-14 BCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:20:26-08:00","id":1016795,"title":"","content":"My favourite Emperor was Julian the Philospher, its a real shame he was murdered.<br /> <br /> I think that would be an interesting time period to play in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:22:05-08:00","id":1016798,"title":"","content":"Which gameline would work best for the distant wilds of Britannia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:17:40-08:00","id":1016822,"title":"","content":"Hunter. You can have them as both natives and Romans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T18:23:06-08:00","id":1016852,"title":"","content":"Or Werewolves - Britain is full of Celts, and they were clear animists. As setting from <b>Dark Eras Companion</b> will show - Romans will have their own Uratha. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-14-2016, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T21:42:52-08:00","id":1016908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1016852#post1016852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Werewolves - Britain is full of Celts, and they were clear animists. As setting from Dark Eras Companion will show - Romans will have their own Uratha. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It will show a wee bit more than that, I hope! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T23:07:54-08:00","id":1016924,"title":"","content":"Add some fae to mix, and you got nice Ancient Britain setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:10:50-08:00","id":1017073,"title":"","content":"You could do an interesting game of Awakening in Britannia. Diamond magi using the conquest to stamp out and assimilate the native magi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:33:05-08:00","id":1019004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015610#post1015610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a half-finished Vigil for Rome project I should reopen.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> I replaced the official version of the Aves Minerva because I found them too much &quot;generic Roman pagans&quot; which works when they're the only Hunter group in the setting, but if they're sharing it with other Roman Hunters they need to be more distinct. Quick run down of the groups I decided to focus on...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Compacts</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Aves Minerva: Plebs and Freemen defenders of the streets of the city. More like the Union than any other modern Compact. They've always been patriotically dedicated to the gods of the city, but debate rages over the admittance of Christians.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Mos Maiorum: Patricians protecting the honor of their families from the blight of the walking dead or other accursed stigmas</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Vox Martyom: Heretical Christians of the Agonistici tradition, who believe martyrdom is the only path to salvation. As the state doesn't serve that purpose anymore post-Constantine, they turn their attention to the unholy forces in the shadows</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Conspiracies</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Collegia Chironos: A mystery cult primarily made up of educated Greek slaves, seeking knowledge of the medical and mystical</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Ieros Dromos: Nicean Christians answerable to Constantinople, breaking the power of the Gnostic witches and the cults of pagan horrors to save the souls of the masses</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Lux Mithrae: a Conspiracy within the Legions wielding consecrated blood of the bull against supernatural foes of the Empire (this is where the Red Rites move)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Other groups (like the Ascending Ones who are the premier Hunters in the Parthian Empire at this point) get some sidebar attention.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>How would you feel about a Compact similar to your take on the Aves Minerva (who I still believe should remain a Conspiracy with possible ties to the Strix), but instead focused on slaves and <i>libertini</i> who protect themselves from both mortal and supernatural abuses? With no one looking out for the lowest of the empire, they must band together, and form a more conspiratorial Night Watch who can reach the sands of the arena and the households of the patricians alike.<br /> <br /> And if you wanted to toss out or revive a Vigil for Rome thread, I'd be all for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:33:05-08:00","id":1019005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.c