ystical</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Ieros Dromos: Nicean Christians answerable to Constantinople, breaking the power of the Gnostic witches and the cults of pagan horrors to save the souls of the masses</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">- Lux Mithrae: a Conspiracy within the Legions wielding consecrated blood of the bull against supernatural foes of the Empire (this is where the Red Rites move)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Other groups (like the Ascending Ones who are the premier Hunters in the Parthian Empire at this point) get some sidebar attention.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>How would you feel about a Compact similar to your take on the Aves Minerva (who I still believe should remain a Conspiracy with possible ties to the Strix), but instead focused on slaves and <i>libertini</i> who protect themselves from both mortal and supernatural abuses? With no one looking out for the lowest of the empire, they must band together, and form a more conspiratorial Night Watch who can reach the sands of the arena and the households of the patricians alike.<br /> <br /> And if you wanted to toss out or revive a Vigil for Rome thread, I'd be all for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:22:52-08:00","id":1019104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1015568#post1015568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun Fact: Changeling 1E posited the Seasonal Courts officially started at some time in the Roman Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would placed creation of Seasonal Courts on early Roman Empire. Republican Lost would have problem with Monarchs rule and mix of Germania cultures seasonal beliefs would catalyze into following Seasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It looks like start of Roman Empire would be great crossover place for <b>Mage/Changeling</b> Dark Era! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:25:53-08:00","id":1019105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1019104#post1019104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would placed creation of Seasonal Courts on early Roman Empire. Republican Lost would have problem with Monarchs rule and mix of Germania cultures seasonal beliefs would catalyze into following Seasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It looks like start of Roman Empire would be great crossover place for <b>Mage/Changeling</b> Dark Era! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>God, that could be a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T00:03:36-08:00","id":1019123,"title":"","content":"Cities I want to see featured in The Crossover Chronicle:<br /> - Tokyo<br /> - Rome<br /> - Maybe others? Or just more wordcount for the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T00:32:50-08:00","id":1019125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015553-rome-for-everyone?p=1019123#post1019123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cities I want to see featured in The Crossover Chronicle:<br /> - Tokyo<br /> - Rome<br /> - Maybe others? Or just more wordcount for the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paris, from before even the Rose Courts were written, was a space in my head for what would be my first crossover game. Since then, expanding on stuff in the background, it has become a rat's nest of metaphysical intersectionality problems like &quot;Maybe I shouldn't develop my ritualistic Hedge Gate in what is also basically an Avernian Gate&quot;, &quot;Maybe we shouldn't have put a Strix attracting line in the middle of a whole section of the city thriving on sacred geometry resonant with Sekhem&quot;, and &quot;Maybe Christians shouldn't listen to every angel that tells them to 'kill' a Spirit Goddess and thus consign it to the Underworld in a state of quantum contradiction that is probably poisoning everything.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a work in progress and probably way too much for Crossover Chronicle, but I'd like to begin more of the threads there.","signatur